AArch64 deque-popsteal-aarch64-relaxed
(* Chase-Lev deque pop/steal Dekker interlock — POSITIVE CONTROL (ordering
 * DELIBERATELY WEAKENED: plain STR/LDR, and the claiming RMW is a plain CAS
 * with no acquire/release). Proves the encoding exercises the store->load
 * reorder and that STLR/LDAR/CASAL are load-bearing: with plain accesses both
 * sides can miss each other (owner and thief take the same item). Under
 * aarch64.cat this MUST be Sometimes/Allowed. *)
{
0:X1=bottom; 0:X3=top;
1:X3=top; 1:X5=bottom;
}
 P0              | P1               ;
 MOV W0,#1       | MOV W1,#0        ;
 STR W0,[X1]     | MOV W2,#1        ;
 LDR W2,[X3]     | CAS W1,W2,[X3]   ;
                 | LDR W4,[X5]      ;
exists
(0:X2=0 /\ 1:X4=0)
